  "definition": "A stochastic differential equation (SDE) is a differential equation in which one or more terms incorporate a stochastic process, typically Brownian motion or white noise, making the solution itself a stochastic process. SDEs generalise ordinary differential equations by including a diffusion term driven by a Wiener process, and their solutions are interpreted via Ito or Stratonovich calculus. SDEs are foundational in financial mathematics, physics, biology, and machine learning \u2014 particularly in score-based generative modelling and diffusion models.",
